    "difficultyReason": "The student must recognise from context that more pumps means less time, so t=k/n. They then find k=36, evaluate twice, and explain that doubling n halves t because nt is constant. Choosing the inverse model without being told it is the main extra demand over p20-q1, where the equation is given. The final explanation asks for a short interpretation of the constant product. It is lighter than p21-q4-block, which adds table and graph work and unit conversion.",
